            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0690" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v01/pg668"/>

                <head>279. Letter From Secretary of State Rusk to the British Ambassador (Ormsby Gore)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d279-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1961-11-25">November 25, 1961</date>.</hi></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear David:</hi> I have
                    considered carefully the points you raised in your note of November 17<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d279-f2"/> referring to our assistance to the Government of
                    VietNam.</p>
                <p>I agree with you that we should try to see to it that our efforts to assist the
                    Vietnamese Government do not reduce the chances for a negotiated settlement of
                    the Laotian problem at Geneva. I also agree that we want to avoid any publicity
                    which would be needlessly provocative.</p>
                <pb facs="0691" n="669" xml:id="pg669"/>
                <p>At the same time it seems to me that we cannot fail to take immediate action
                    needed to lay a foundation for the prospective program of expanded assistance to
                    VietNam. The contemplated publication of the “Jorden Report” exposing and
                    documenting the North Vietnamese part in the Viet Cong guerrilla war is an
                    essential prelude to the program.</p>
                <p>I believe you will concur that the forthcoming publication is factual, objective
                    and probably understated.</p>
                <p>With appreciation as always for your comments,</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dean</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d279-f3"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
